  "operation": "REPL prompt typed exit without close retains status",
  "observed_scope": "Windows validation/static component observations only; no Linux/macOS applicability or source-build provenance claim",
  "rationale": "The actual public os.exit(37,false) deliberately does not close the state. Instrumented native C registers atexit(checkfinalmem), whose private l_memcontrol.numblocks==0 assertion conflicts with that deliberate process-lifetime choice. Original loslib.c closes only when the second argument is true. Native default and Ada T retain actual status37, exact banner and empty stderr. Native T retains status37/banner but emits the private assertion at2226. No Lua prompt source or C oracle bytes were adapted.",
  "proposed_disposition": "Independent review required: record the exact native-T-only private allocator diagnostic separately from public prompt parity; keep full Ada T and ordinary native counterpart mandatory. No operation may be silently omitted or called passing native T from this proposal.",
